[[Vladimír Franz]] appears insignificant in agency surveys but in November he was the obvious favorite of opinion polls of several different popular news servers and media (Aktuálně.cz,<ref>[http://aktualne.centrum.cz/domaci/grafika/2012/11/06/koho-byste-zvolili-prezidentem-ceske-republiky Koho byste zvolili prezidentem České republiky?], Aktuálně.cz, 6. 11. 2012</ref> Reflex,<ref>Dita Ondrejková: [http://www.reflex.cz/clanek/zpravy/48475/a-prezidentem-z-volby-nanecisto-se-stava-vladimir-franz.html A prezidentem z volby nanečisto se stává... Vladimír Franz!], Reflex.cz, 8. 11. 2012</ref> iDnes.cz<ref>Jan Wirnitzer: [http://zpravy.idnes.cz/ctenari-chteji-za-prezidenta-franze-dbm-/domaci.aspx?c=A121118_125507_domaci_jw Čtenáři vybrali za prezidenta Franze, ve druhém kole získal 56 procent], iDnes.cz, 18. 1. 2012</ref>) as well as of so-called "students' elections"<ref>[http://zpravy.idnes.cz/studenti-cvicne-volili-prezidenta-dt1-/domaci.aspx?c=A121212_122033_domaci_jj Středoškoláci zvolili na Hrad Franze, straničtí kandidáti propadli], iDnes.cz, 12. 12. 2012 jj (Jan Jiřička), hv (Hana Válková)</ref> in all regions and all types of secondary schools.<ref>[http://www.novinky.cz/veda-skoly/287863-proc-zvolili-stredoskolaci-franze-ze-stavajicich-pomeru-jsou-rozcarovani.html Proč zvolili středoškoláci Franze? Ze stávajících poměrů jsou rozčarováni], Novinky.cz, 14. 12. 2012</ref> The current president Klaus expressed fear that his successor would be Franz or Okamura.<ref>Zdeňka Trachtová, Jan Wirnitzer: [http://zpravy.idnes.cz/klaus-o-prime-volbe-prezidenta-dze-/domaci.aspx?c=A121207_115150_domaci_jw Přímá volba se strašně vymstí, řekl Klaus. Obává se Franze či Okamury], iDnes.cz. 7. 12. 2012</ref>

===Disqualified candidates===

The following list includes the candidates who were disqualified after the [[Ministry of Interior of the Czech Republic|Ministry of Interior]] reviewed their petitions assessing that they failed to meet the quorum of minimum of 50,000 popular signatures or twenty MPs in the Chamber of Deputies, or ten MPs in the Senate.

Candidates [[Jana Bobošíková]], [[Vladimír Dlouhý (politician)|Vladimír Dlouhý]], and [[Tomio Okamura]] collected more than 50,000 signatures; however, after checking two samples of each petition and reducing the number of signatures according to the error rate, the number fell below the requirement; accordingly, they were not registered as candidates. Along with the action, the ministry stated that many of Bobošíková's alleged signatories were long dead; while in case of Okamura, the ministry found a large number of fictitious signatories. Both candidates appealed the ministry's decision before the [[Supreme Administrative Court of the Czech Republic|Supreme Administrative Court]], believing that the ministry had used an incorrect method of recount.<ref name="recount" />

On 13 December 2012, the Supreme Administrative Court ruled on the complaints. It ordered that Bobošíková must be registered as a candidate, and rejected the complaints of Dlouhý and Okamura, as even after correcting the error in computation their number of valid signatures still fails to meet the quorum.<ref name="NSS" /> Okamura unsuccessfully challenged the verdict at the [[Constitutional Court of the Czech Republic|Constitutional Court]].<ref name="concourt">{{cite web|url=http://www.concourt.cz/clanek/7599|title=Ústavní soud zamítl stížnost Tomia Okamury k prezidentské volbě|date=4 January 2013|publisher=[[Constitutional Court of the Czech Republic]]|language=cs|access-date=27 January 2013|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://archive.today/20130217030607/http://www.concourt.cz/clanek/7599|archive-date=17 February 2013|df=dmy-all}}</ref>

