===Withdrawn candidate===
Jan Toman from [[Bechyně]] filed his own candidature on 6 November but he attached no petition.<ref>[http://www.mvcr.cz/soubor/toman-pdf.aspx Výzva k odstranění závad na kandidátní listině – Mgr. et Mgr. Jan Toman], Ministerstvo vnitra ČR, 2012-11-13</ref> He was also the attorney of the candidate Karel Světnička, and Karel Světnička was the attorney of Jan Toman. However, a candidate must not be an attorney of any proposer. Jan Světnička surrendered his own candidature on 22 November and remained the attorney of Karel Světnička.<ref>[http://www.mvcr.cz/soubor/karel-svetnicka-pdf.aspx Rozhodnutí o odmítnutí kandidátní listiny nebo o odmítnutí kandidátní listiny, Mgr. et Bc. Karel Světnička], Ministerstvo vnitra ČR, 2012-11-23</ref>

===Other announced candidates===
The following list includes some of the people who announced their candidacy but the proposal was not filed finally. Some of them started to collect petition signatures.
*[[Ladislav Jakl]], [[Party of Free Citizens]], secretary to President [[Václav Klaus]].<ref>{{cite news |url= http://praguemonitor.com/2012/09/24/presidential-candidate-jakl-launches-petition-his-bid |title= Presidential candidate Jakl launches petition for his bid |work= Prague Daily Monitor |agency= ČTK |date= 24 September 2012 |access-date= 24 September 2012 |url-status= dead |archive-url= https://archive.today/20130131174616/http://praguemonitor.com/2012/09/24/presidential-candidate-jakl-launches-petition-his-bid |archive-date= 31 January 2013 |df= dmy-all }}</ref> He won the [[2012 Party of Free Citizens presidential primaries|party's primaries]] but failed to gather enough signatures.
*[[Rut Kolínská]], President of the Mother Centres Network<ref name=spycatcher/>
*[[Karel Randák]], former head of the Czech counter-intelligence<ref name=spycatcher>{{cite news |url= http://praguemonitor.com/2012/09/14/former-chief-spycatcher-running-president |title= Former chief spycatcher running for president |agency= ČTK |work= Prague Daily Monitor |date= 14 September 2012 |access-date= 18 September 2012 |url-status= dead |archive-url= https://archive.today/20130131145527/http://praguemonitor.com/2012/09/14/former-chief-spycatcher-running-president |archive-date= 31 January 2013 |df= dmy-all }}</ref>
*[[Tomáš Vandas]], [[Workers' Party (Czech Republic)|DSSS]]<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.ceskenoviny.cz/domov/volby/zpravy/o-prezidentsky-urad-se-bude-uchazet-nejmene-devet-kandidatu/861471|title=O prezidentský úřad se bude ucházet nejméně devět kandidátů|date=4 November 2012|publisher=České noviny ([[ČTK]])|language=cs|access-date=27 January 2013}}</ref>

===Other possible candidates===
[[Jan Švejnar]] a candidate in [[2008 Czech presidential election|2008 presidential election]] was speculated to be one of possible candidates and he himself admitted that he considers running. He quickly one of the frontrunners according to polls that showed him being the 2nd strongest candidate. His support decreased by the time and he fell to 3rd or 4th place. Švejnar eventually said in September 2012 that he won't run.<ref>{{cite web|last1=Šráfeldová|first1=Milena|title=Jan Švejnar ukončil dohady, nebude kandidovat v prezidentských volbách|url=http://www.radio.cz/cz/rubrika/udalosti/jan-svejnar-ukoncil-dohady-nebude-kandidovat-v-prezidentskych-volbach|website=Radio Praha|date=12 September 2012 |access-date=18 July 2016}}</ref>

[[Vladimír Remek]] was offered presidential nomination by [[Communist Party of Bohemia and Moravia]].<ref name="Komunisté oslovili kvůli volbě na Hrad Remka. Straníci navrhli i Filipa">{{cite web|title=Komunisté oslovili kvůli volbě na Hrad Remka. Straníci navrhli i Filipa|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/kandidatem-komunistu-na-hrad-muze-byt-kosmonaut-remek-ppz-/domaci.aspx?c=A121015_132527_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=10 May 2017|date=15 October 2012}}</ref> He rejected his own party's offer.<ref name="Remek odmítl nabídku komunistů kandidovat na prezidenta">{{cite web|title=Remek odmítl nabídku komunistů kandidovat na prezidenta|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/vladimir-remek-nebude-kandidovat-na-prezidenta-flt-/domaci.aspx?c=A121025_164319_domaci_zt|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=10 May 2017|date=25 October 2012}}</ref>

==Primaries==
===Civic Democratic Party (ODS)===
[[File:Prez-primarky-ODS-2012.png|thumb|right|ODS Primaries results by districts]]
{{Main|2012 Civic Democratic Party presidential primaries}}
[[Civic Democratic Party (Czech Republic)|Civic Democratic Party]] held primary elections to decide who will become party's candidate. Primaries were held from end of April 2012 to 28 June 2012. Vice-Chairman of Senate [[Přemysl Sobotka]] faced MEP [[Evžen Tošenovský]]. Sobotka received 61% of votes and won party's nomination. Primaries suffered of low voter turnout.<ref>{{cite web|title=Kandidátem ODS na prezidenta je Přemysl Sobotka|url=https://www.novinky.cz/domaci/271751-kandidatem-ods-na-prezidenta-je-premysl-sobotka.html|website=Novinky.cz|date=28 June 2012 |access-date=25 March 2017|language=cs}}</ref>

===Czech Social Democratic Party (ČSSD)===
{{Main|2012 Czech Social Democratic Party presidential primaries}}
[[Czech Social Democratic Party]] held primaries in May 2012.  The primaries were indirect, with only members of the party's Central Executive Committee able to vote. [[Jiří Dienstbier Jr.]] was expected to face [[Jan Švejnar]]. Švejnar withdrawn from primaries before voting took place and Dienstbier received the nomination on 19 May 2012.<ref>{{cite web|title=ČSSD má kandidáta na Hrad: Stal se jím Jiří Dienstbier|url=http://www.blesk.cz/clanek/zpravy-politika/174610/cssd-ma-kandidata-na-hrad-stal-se-jim-jiri-dienstbier.html|website=Blesk.cz|date=19 May 2012 |access-date=25 March 2017}}</ref>

===Party of Free Citizens (Svobodní) ===
{{Main|2012 Party of Free Citizens presidential primaries}}
The [[Party of Free Citizens]] held presidential primaries in June 2012. [[Ladislav Jakl]], the secretary of President Václav Klaus, was the only candidate.<ref>{{cite web|title=Svobodní: Naším jediným kandidátem na prezidenta je Jakl|url=http://www.tyden.cz/rubriky/domaci/svobodni-nasim-jedinym-kandidatem-na-prezidenta-je-jakl_236832.html|website=TÝDEN.cz|access-date=25 March 2017|date=7 June 2012}}</ref> Jakl received 88% of votes and won the nomination but the party failed to gather enough signatures and Jakl could not participate in the election.<ref>{{cite web|title=Klausův poradce Jakl dostal podporu pro kandidaturu na Hrad|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/jakl-dostal-podporu-svobodnych-pri-kandidature-na-hrad-pgg-/domaci.aspx?c=A120617_181254_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=25 March 2017|date=17 June 2012}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Jakl podpisy nezískal. Měl jsem se sběru věnovat usilovněji, říká {{!}} Domov|url=http://www.lidovky.cz/jakl-podpisy-neziskal-na-hrad-vsak-miri-fischerova-a-okamura-plz-/zpravy-domov.aspx?c=A121106_102900_ln_domov_kim|website=Lidovky.cz|access-date=25 March 2017|date=6 November 2012}}</ref>

===Public Affairs (VV)===
[[Public Affairs (political party)|Public Affairs]] also intended to choose its candidate in presidential primaries. [[Jan Švejnar]] was mentioned by Vít Bárta as a possible candidate.<ref>{{cite web|title=ODS má tři jména pro Hrad, přibyl Tošenovský. Rozhodnout mohou primárky|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/ods-ma-tri-jmena-pro-hrad-pribyl-tosenovsky-rozhodnout-mohou-primarky-1mq-/domaci.aspx?c=A120221_105512_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=27 March 2017|date=21 February 2012}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=VV vyberou kandidáta na Hrad v primárkách. Bártovi se líbí Švejnar|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/vv-vyberou-kandidata-na-hrad-v-primarkach-bartovi-se-libi-svejnar-ph4-/domaci.aspx?c=A111021_133801_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=27 March 2017|date=21 October 2011}}</ref> Švejnar himself didn't say that he would agree with nomination by the party.<ref>{{cite web|title=ZVĚŘINA: Prezidentský poker {{!}} Názory|url=http://www.lidovky.cz/zverina-prezidentsky-poker-dp9-/nazory.aspx?c=A111023_133323_ln_nazory_sk|website=Lidovky.cz|access-date=27 March 2017|date=23 October 2011}}</ref> Leader of Public Affairs [[Radek John]] said that he would support [[Jan Fischer (politician)|Jan Fischer]].<ref>{{cite web|title=ČSSD vybrala dva kandidáty na Hrad: Dienstbiera a Švejnara|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/cssd-vybrala-dva-kandidaty-na-hrad-dienstbiera-a-svejnara-pe3-/domaci.aspx?c=A120218_084445_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=27 March 2017|date=18 February 2012}}</ref> Primaries never happened and [[Tomio Okamura]] was later speculated to be possible candidate of Public Affairs.<ref>{{cite web|title=Okamura potvrdil, že chce na Hrad. Sbírá podpisy a lobbuje v parlamentu|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/tomio-okamura-kandidatura-na-prezidenta-fd3-/domaci.aspx?c=A121002_203735_domaci_brd|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=27 March 2017|date=3 October 2012}}</ref>

==Campaign==
[[File:Táňa Fischerová - Superdebata prezidentských kandidátů 2.jpg|thumbnail|Presidential debate on [[Czech Television]] (ČT)]]
{{multiple image
| align     = right
| direction = horizontal
| width     = 150
| footer    = A sample of a ballot paper of [[Miloš Zeman]] and [[Karel Schwarzenberg]] used for the first round of the presidential election.
| image1    = CZ-PR2013-6-Zeman.jpg
| image2    = CZ-PR2013-9-Schwarzenberg.jpg
}}
Zeman and Fischer were leading in the polls, but Schwarzenberg's campaign ended on a higher note with a crowd of about 10,000 people at a rally in Prague.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.ceskatelevize.cz/ct24/domaci/210326-prezidentska-kampan-vrcholi-dnes-hlavne-kulturne/|title=Prezidentská kampaň vrcholí, dnes hlavně kulturně|date=9 January 2013|publisher=Czech Television|language=cs|access-date=27 January 2013}}</ref> Zeman said of the runoff: "It will be a presidential race between a candidate for the left and a candidate for the right. We'll start from scratch for the second round;" Schwarzenberg said of his campaign that he would make the Czech Republic "a successful country." Vladimír Franz called his campaign "a success."<ref>{{cite web|url=http://zpravy.ihned.cz/politika/c1-59111720-vladimir-franz-vytvorili-jsme-energii-nesmime-se-ponorit-do-tmy|title=Vladimír Franz: Vytvořili jsme energii. Nesmíme se ponořit do tmy|date=12 January 2013|work=[[Hospodářské noviny]]|publisher=iHNED|access-date=27 January 2013}}</ref>

===First round===
[[Miloš Zeman]] and [[Jan Fischer (politician)|Jan Fischer]] stated they would run if the election is direct.<ref name="Do přímé volby bych určitě šel, přihlásil se Fischer o Hrad">{{cite web|title=Do přímé volby bych určitě šel, přihlásil se Fischer o Hrad|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/volba-prezidenta-0ej-/domaci.aspx?c=A110207_165854_krimi_jw|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=7 February 2011}}</ref> [[2008 Czech presidential election|2008 presidential candidate]] [[Jan Švejnar]] was also speculated as a candidate.<ref name="Lidé by na Hrad zvolili Švejnara. Místo Sobotky chtějí mezi kandidáty Zemana">{{cite web|title=Lidé by na Hrad zvolili Švejnara. Místo Sobotky chtějí mezi kandidáty Zemana|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/lide-by-na-hrad-zvolili-svejnara-misto-sobotky-chteji-mezi-kandidaty-zemana-1bg-/domaci.aspx?c=A101227_204004_domaci_brm|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=28 December 2010}}</ref> Zeman's [[Party of Civic Rights]] started petition campaign for direct election on 29 June 2011.<ref name="Zemanovci rozjeli petiční akci za přímou volbu prezidenta a starostů">{{cite web|title=Zemanovci rozjeli petiční akci za přímou volbu prezidenta a starostů|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/zemanovci-rozjeli-peticni-akci-za-primou-volbu-prezidenta-a-starostu-1kl-/domaci.aspx?c=A110629_115028_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=29 June 2011}}</ref> Petition was signed by more than 100,000 people as of October 2011.<ref name="Zemanovu petici za přímou volbu na Hrad podpořilo přes 100 tisíc lidí">{{cite web|title=Zemanovu petici za přímou volbu na Hrad podpořilo přes 100 tisíc lidí|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/zemanovu-petici-za-primou-volbu-na-hrad-podporilo-pres-100-tisic-lidi-1ps-/domaci.aspx?c=A111004_095744_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=4 October 2011}}</ref> Direct election was accepted by parliament on 8 February 2012.<ref>{{cite web|title=Přímá volba prezidenta prošla. Lidé sami vyberou už Klausova nástupce|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/prima-volba-prezidenta-prosla-lide-sami-vyberou-uz-klausova-nastupce-1kk-/domaci.aspx?c=A120208_135604_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=8 February 2012}}</ref>

[[Karel Schwarzenberg]] announced his candidature on 22 October 2011.<ref name="Schwarzenberg bude kandidovat na prezidenta">{{cite web|title=Schwarzenberg bude kandidovat na prezidenta|url=https://www.novinky.cz/domaci/248228-schwarzenberg-bude-kandidovat-na-prezidenta.html|website=Novinky.cz|date=22 October 2011 |access-date=31 May 2017|language=cs}}</ref>

Former prime minister of the Czech Republic [[Jan Fischer (politician)|Jan Fischer]] announced his candidature on 7 January 2012.<ref name="Přímé volby prezidenta se zúčastním, prohlásil expremiér Fischer">{{cite web|title=Přímé volby prezidenta se zúčastním, prohlásil expremiér Fischer|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/prime-volby-prezidenta-se-zucastnim-prohlasil-expremier-fischer-pyu-/domaci.aspx?c=A120106_195834_domaci_brm|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=7 January 2012}}</ref> [[Jana Bobošíková]] announced her candidature on 9 February 2012. [[Miloš Zeman]] stated that he will officially announce his candidature when he gathers enough signatures.<ref name="Do přímé volby na Hrad přibyl třetí jasný kandidát, Jana Bobošíková">{{cite web|title=Do přímé volby na Hrad přibyl třetí jasný kandidát, Jana Bobošíková|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/do-prime-volby-na-hrad-pribyl-treti-jasny-kandidat-jana-bobosikova-1co-/domaci.aspx?c=A120209_112959_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=9 February 2012}}</ref>

Miloš Zeman announced his candidature on 14 February 2012. [[Party of Civic Rights]] started to gather signatures for him.<ref name="Miloš Zeman po deseti letech zkusí znovu dobýt Hrad">{{cite web|title=Miloš Zeman po deseti letech zkusí znovu dobýt Hrad|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/milos-zeman-po-deseti-letech-zkusi-znovu-dobyt-hrad-fhe-/domaci.aspx?c=A120214_123858_domaci_jw|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=14 February 2012}}</ref> His presidential bid received support from [[LEV 21]] and some politicians of [[Czech Social Democratic Party]] (ČSSD).<ref>{{cite web|title=Zeman na Hradě by se líbil Paroubkovi, přímluvce má i ve vedení ČSSD|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/zeman-na-hrade-by-se-libil-paroubkovi-primluvce-ma-i-ve-vedeni-cssd-p9s-/domaci.aspx?c=A120216_142321_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=16 February 2012}}</ref> ČSSD later decided to stand its own candidate [[Jiří Dienstbier Jr.]]

Jan Fischer became front-runner in early 2012. [[Jan Švejnar]] was considered his main rival. [[Miloš Zeman]] was third strongest candidate according to polls. Švejnar himself was at the time waiting if he receives support of Czech Social Democratic Party<ref>{{cite web|title=Zemana chce na Hradě víc lidí než Schwarzenberga, ukázal průzkum|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/novym-prezidentem-by-se-stal-fischer-zeman-je-treti-fxy-/domaci.aspx?c=A120314_173102_domaci_wlk|website=iDNES.cz| date=14 March 2012 |access-date=31 May 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Švejnar napíná ČSSD. Vyčkává, zda ho strana podpoří na Hrad|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/svejnar-napina-cssd-vyckava-zda-ho-strana-podpori-na-hrad-pe4-/domaci.aspx?c=A120316_122047_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=16 March 2012}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Zeman ani Okamura by se podle průzkumu na Hrad neprobojovali|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/favority-prime-volby-prezidenta-jsou-fischer-a-svejnar-piw-/domaci.aspx?c=A120414_090604_domaci_jj|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=14 April 2012}}</ref>

Miloš Zeman started gathering signatures on 21 March 2012 when he launched his presidential campaign.<ref name="Zeman začal boj o Hrad, lidem dá do schránek leták se svým životopisem">{{cite web|title=Zeman začal boj o Hrad, lidem dá do schránek leták se svým životopisem|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/zeman-se-pustil-do-boje-o-hrad-dja-/domaci.aspx?c=A120321_122026_domaci_jj|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=21 March 2012}}</ref> Jan Fischer started his campaign on 2 April 2012.<ref>{{cite web|title=Fischer neoficiálně zahájil prezidentskou kampaň. Zpoza květináče|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/fischer-zahajil-prezidentskou-kampan-d83-/domaci.aspx?c=A120402_162823_domaci_jw|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=2 April 2012}}</ref>

Jan Švejnar withdrew from [[2012 Czech Social Democratic Party presidential primaries|ČSSD primaries]] on 2 May 2012 and decided to run as independent.<ref>{{cite web|title=Švejnar nechce na Hrad za ČSSD, ale sám za sebe, přiznal Sobotka|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/otazniky-kolem-svejnarovy-kandidatury-na-hrad-za-cssd-pp5-/domaci.aspx?c=A120502_174613_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=2 May 2012}}</ref> Czech Social Democratic Party then nominated [[Jiří Dienstbier Jr.]]

Zeman grew in polls and in May 2012 he caught up with Jan Švejnar in polls. He also received signatures of 10 senators which meant he doesn't need 50,000 signatures.<ref>{{cite web|title=Zeman dohání Švejnara, bojují o druhé místo v prezidentské volbě|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/zeman-je-treti-v-pruzkumu-prezidentskych-kandidatu-fyk-/domaci.aspx?c=A120506_170628_domaci_brm|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=6 May 2012}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Šance Zemana na Hrad rostou. Má podpisy senátorů i rostoucí důvěru lidí|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/zeman-ma-vetsi-sanci-byt-prezidentem-dv5-/domaci.aspx?c=A120507_124216_domaci_jj|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=7 May 2012}}</ref> Zeman gathered required number of signatures by the end of June 2012.<ref>{{cite web|title=Zeman předběhl soupeře, má 50 tisíc podpisů. Kampaň bude bez Šloufa|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/zeman-uz-ma-50-tisic-podpisu-aby-mohl-kandidovat-na-hrad-pf8-/domaci.aspx?c=A120626_095513_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=26 June 2012}}</ref> Polls in June 2012 indicated that Miloš Zeman became Fischer's main rival.<ref>{{cite web|title=Zeman v průzkumu předstihl Švejnara. O Hrad by se utkal s Fischerem|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/podle-medianu-ma-zeman-skoro-stejne-sance-jako-svejnar-ppp-/domaci.aspx?c=A120606_174930_domaci_mku|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=6 June 2012}}</ref>

[[Civic Democratic Party (Czech Republic)|Civic Democratic Party]] nominated [[Přemysl Sobotka]] on 28 June 2012 when Sobotka won the [[2012 Civic Democratic Party presidential primaries|party's presidential primaries]]. Sobotka stated that his campaign will cost 8 million Korunas.<ref>{{cite web|title=ODS nasadí do boje o Hrad Přemysla Sobotku, k favoritům volby nepatří|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/ods-do-prezidentske-volby-nasadi-premysla-sobotku-fwl-/domaci.aspx?c=A120628_062538_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=28 June 2012}}</ref> Candidate of [[Czech Social Democratic Party]] [[Jiří Dienstbier Jr.]] stated on the other hand that his campaign will cost tens of million Korunas. Dienstbier came third according to one of polls.<ref>{{cite web|title=Dienstbier má průzkum, že poráží Zemana. Utratí desítky milionů|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/dienstbier-predstavil-kampan-pro-volbu-prezidenta-f8a-/domaci.aspx?c=A120629_144845_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=29 June 2012}}</ref>

Jan Fischer started to fully pursue his campaign on 9 July. He was supported by businessman Jaromír Soukup.<ref>{{cite web|title=Fischer končí v Londýně, na Hrad mu pomáhá mediální magnát Soukup|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/prezidentsky-kandidat-fischer-konci-v-londynske-bance-ppr-/domaci.aspx?c=A120620_113629_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=9 July 2012}}</ref> Fischer was still front-runner at the time while Miloš Zeman was his main competition. Jan Švejnar who was originally considered the main rival of Fischer was losing in polls due to his indecisiveness.<ref>{{cite web|title=Švejnarovi váhání škodí, míní experti. Poslanci řekl, že na Hrad chce|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/svejnarovi-muze-vahani-u-volicu-uskodit-fd8-/domaci.aspx?c=A120723_140013_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=23 July 2012}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Fischer versus Zeman, tvrdí průzkum. Švejnarovy šance slábnou|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/favority-prezidentske-volby-jsou-fischer-a-zeman-f7u-/domaci.aspx?c=A120725_103017_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=25 July 2012}}</ref>

[[Vladimír Franz]] announced his candidature on 30 July 2012.<ref>{{cite web|title=Potetovaný umělec Franz oznámil na Facebooku zájem o Hrad|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/vladimir-franz-kandiduje-na-prezidenta-d9d-/domaci.aspx?c=A120730_220626_domaci_ert|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=30 July 2012}}</ref>

[[Přemysl Sobotka]] started his campaign on 17 August 2012.<ref>{{cite web|title=Sobotka rozjel kampaň: poslance volme přímo a k euru buďme opatrní|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/kancelar-premysla-sobotky-dcx-/domaci.aspx?c=A120817_093941_domaci_jw|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=17 August 2012}}</ref> Jan Fischer gathered 50,000 signatures by the end of August 2012.<ref>{{cite web|title=Fischer nasbíral 50 tisíc podpisů a může kandidovat na prezidenta|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/fischer-nasbiral-50-tisic-podpisu-pro-kandidaturu-na-hrad-p2h-/domaci.aspx?c=A120827_124127_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=27 August 2012}}</ref>

Švejnar announced on 11 September 2012 that he won't run and endorsed Jan Fischer. [[Tomio Okamura]] started to gather signatures at the time<ref>{{cite web|title=Švejnar vzdal boj o Hrad, fanoušci Okamury naopak začali sbírat podpisy|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/svejnar-se-nezucastni-prime-volby-prezidenta-fo3-/domaci.aspx?c=A120911_102244_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=11 September 2012}}</ref> On 14 September 2012, Jan Fischer officially launched his campaign. He defined himself against Zeman and stated that "Czech Republic isn't a burnt land" reminding Zeman's statements from 1990s. He promised that Czechs won't be ashamed of him as a president.<ref>{{cite web|title=Fischer zahájil kampaň. Česko není spálená země, vymezil se proti Zemanovi|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/fischer-zahajil-kampan-0b3-/domaci.aspx?c=A120914_125847_domaci_maq|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=14 September 2012}}</ref> Švejnar's withdrawal led to Fischer's growth in polls.<ref name="Švejnarovo odstoupení nahrálo Fischerovi, protestní hlasy sbírá Franz">{{cite web|title=Švejnarovo odstoupení nahrálo Fischerovi, protestní hlasy sbírá Franz|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/svejnar-nahral-fischerovi-a-zemanovi-dsu-/domaci.aspx?c=A120917_155115_domaci_jw|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=17 September 2012}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Fischer v prezidentském průzkumu posílil, Okamura je opět třetí|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/prezidentska-volba-fischer-okamura-d6z-/domaci.aspx?c=A121015_104331_domaci_jw|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=15 October 2012}}</ref>

[[Green Party (Czech Republic)|Green Party]] supported [[Táňa Fischerová]] for the election. Greens started gathering signatures for her on 27 September 2012.<ref>{{cite web|title=Na Hrad nepatří Fischer, ale Fischerová, řekli zelení. Sbírají podpisy|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/zeleni-podporili-jako-kandidatku-na-hrad-tanu-fischerovou-p3h-/domaci.aspx?c=A120927_125045_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=27 September 2012}}</ref> Jana Bobošíková gathered enough signatures on 29 September 2012.<ref>{{cite web|title=Bobošíková má podpisy na boj o Hrad, za útok na Klause chce demise|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/bobosikova-ma-50-tisic-podpisu-dj9-/domaci.aspx?c=A120929_083716_domaci_jw|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=29 September 2012}}</ref> [[Vladimír Dlouhý (politician)|Vladimír Dlouhý]] and [[Zuzana Roithová]] announced on 1 October 2012 that they are getting closer to required number of signatures.<ref>{{cite web|title=Blížíme se 50 tisícům podpisů, hlásí zájemci o Hrad Dlouhý a Roithová|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/uz-se-blizime-k-50-tisicum-hlasi-tymy-dlouheho-a-roithove-pjs-/domaci.aspx?c=A121001_151905_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=1 October 2012}}</ref>

[[Tomio Okamura]] announced candidature on 3 October 2012. He also started to gather signatures.<ref name="zpravy_2012-10-03">{{cite web|title=Okamura potvrdil, že chce na Hrad. Sbírá podpisy a lobbuje v parlamentu|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/tomio-okamura-kandidatura-na-prezidenta-fd3-/domaci.aspx?c=A121002_203735_domaci_brd|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=3 October 2012}}</ref> [[Zuzana Roithová]] gathered enough signatures on the same day.<ref name="zpravy_2012-10-03"/> [[Vladimír Dlouhý (politician)|Vladimír Dlouhý]] announced that he gathered 50,000 signatures on 5 October 2012.<ref>{{cite web|title=Už mám 50 tisíc podpisů, říká Dlouhý. Reformu penzí by odložil|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/rozhovor-s-kandidatem-na-hrad-dlouhym-ktery-sehnal-50-tisic-pnn-/domaci.aspx?c=A121005_114350_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=5 October 2012}}</ref>

As of 5 November 2012, [[Miloš Zeman]], [[Vladimír Dlouhý (politician)|Vladimír Dlouhý]], [[Jan Fischer (politician)|Jan Fischer]], [[Jana Bobošíková]], [[Zuzana Roithová]], [[Vladimír Franz]] and [[Tomio Okamura]] reportedly had enough signatures to run. [[Táňa Fischerová]] and [[Pavel Kořán]] were close to the number while [[Klára Samková]] and [[Ladislav Jakl]] was unlikely get enough signatures.<ref>{{cite web|title=Franz překvapil, do boje o Hrad jde s 88 388 podpisy. Uspěl i Okamura|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/okamura-ma-50-tisic-podpisu-dcp-/domaci.aspx?c=A121105_111233_domaci_jw|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=5 November 2012}}</ref>

Nominations were closed on 6 November 2012. There were 11 candidates who met required conditions. [[Miloš Zeman]], [[Jan Fischer (politician)|Jan Fischer]], [[Vladimír Franz]], [[Zuzana Roithová]], [[Tomio Okamura]], [[Táňa Fischerová]], [[Vladimír Dlouhý (politician)|Vladimír Dlouhý]] and [[Jana Bobošíková]] gathered over 50,000 signatures while [[Jiří Dienstbier Jr.|Jiří Dienstbier]], [[Přemysl Sobotka]] and [[Karel Schwarzenberg]] received parliamentary nomination.<ref>{{cite web|title=Česko zná všechny kandidáty na prezidenta. Jakl a Švejnar neprošli|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/jakl-nebude-kandidat-na-prezidenta-d5f-/domaci.aspx?c=A120131_125323_domaci_jj|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=6 November 2012}}</ref> On 23 November, Bobošíková, Dlouhý and Okamura were disqualified from the election due to invalid signatures.<ref>{{cite web|title=Vyřazení některých kandidátů může odložit přímou volbu prezidenta|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/vyrazeni-nekterych-kandidatu-muze-ohrozit-termin-prime-pk2-/domaci.aspx?c=A121122_130808_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=22 November 2012}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Okamurovi škrtli 26 tisíc podpisů, dál nejde ani Bobošíková a Dlouhý|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/ministerstvo-vnitra-vyradilo-kandidaty-z-prime-volby-prezidenta-p99-/domaci.aspx?c=A121123_114054_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=23 November 2012}}</ref> Bobošíková was returned to the election after recount on 13 December 2012.<ref>{{cite web|title=Bobošíkovou vrátil soud do boje o Hrad. Okamura a Dlouhý neuspěli|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/rozhodnuti-soudu-o-vyrazenych-kandidatech-na-hrad-fss-/domaci.aspx?c=A121213_084356_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=13 December 2012}}</ref>

According to polls in November 2012, a gap between Fischer and Zeman started to shrink.<ref>{{cite web|title=Zeman v boji o Hrad dohání Fischera. Posílili i Franz a Fischerová|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/prima-volba-prezidenta-fischer-a-zeman-dhm-/domaci.aspx?c=A121108_124412_domaci_jpl|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=8 November 2012}}</ref> Zeman took lead in January 2013 after debates held prior to voting.<ref>{{cite web|title=Poslední předvolební průzkum ovládl Zeman, volil by ho každý čtvrtý|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/posledni-predvolebni-pruzkum-prezidentske-volby-fv7-/domaci.aspx?c=A130106_204849_domaci_hro|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=7 January 2013}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Zeman u sázkových společností předběhl Fischera, poprvé má lepší kurz|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/sazkari-zmenili-kurz-na-zemana-je-favoritem-voleb-fvc-/domaci.aspx?c=A130106_121702_domaci_hv|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=6 January 2013}}</ref>

Voting took place on 11 and 12 January 2013. Zeman and [[Karel Schwarzenberg]] qualified for the second round. Jan Fischer was surprisingly eliminated when he received only 16% of votes and came third. Zeman received only 40,000 votes more than Schwarzenberg.<ref>{{cite web|title=Zeman a Schwarzenberg se utkají o Hrad, dělilo je jen 41 tisíc hlasů|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/prezidentske-volby-2013-0uh-/domaci.aspx?c=A130112_135527_domaci_jav|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=12 January 2013}}</ref> Chances of both candidates in second round were considered balanced.<ref>{{cite web|title=ANALÝZA: Ve Schwarzenbergovi má teď Zeman těžšího soupeře, než tušil|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/jake-maji-pred-druhym-kolem-sance-zeman-a-schwarzenberg-pga-/domaci.aspx?c=A130112_181455_domaci_kop|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=12 January 2013}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=KOMENTÁŘ: Schwarzenberg může Zemana porazit, když nepoleví|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/komentar-k-prezidentskym-volbam-do5-/domaci.aspx?c=A130112_160609_domaci_klm|website=iDNES.cz|access-date=31 May 2017|date=12 January 2013}}</ref>

===Second round===
[[File:Prezidentské volby 2013, volební místnost.jpg|thumb|Second round at Štěpánská Elementary, [[Prague]], Czech Republic]]
The campaign for the second round started with the agreement of both candidates, [[Miloš Zeman]] and [[Karel Schwarzenberg]], not to attack each other and to conduct their campaign in a civil manner.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.lidovky.cz/knizata-zdegenerovala-a-dalsi-perly-dbz-/zpravy-domov.aspx?c=A130119_112505_ln_domov_khu|title=Knížata zdegenerovala, kostlivci z privatizace. Kampaň víří ostrá slova|date=20 January 2013|work=[[Lidové noviny]]|publisher=lidovky.cz|language=cs|access-date=22 January 2013}}</ref> However, when, in the second debate in the [[Czech Television]] held on 17 January 2013, Karel Schwarzenberg stated that the [[expulsion of Germans from Czechoslovakia]] after [[World War II]] would be today (in the 21st century) considered a war crime and [[Czechoslovak government-in-exile|the creators]] of the [[Beneš decrees]] (a series of laws dealing inter alia with the status of ethnic Germans and Hungarians in postwar Czechoslovakia in connection with Article 12 of the [[Potsdam Agreement]]) would be probably judged by the [[International Criminal Court|Hague Tribunal]] as war criminals, Zeman responded as following: ''"... he who marks (...) one of the presidents of Czechoslovakia as a war criminal, speaks as a "[[Sudeten Germans|sudeťák]]"'' [Sudeten German] ''and not as the president"''.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://zpravy.ihned.cz/politika/c1-59149540-zeman-a-schwarzenberg-se-stretli-v-druhe-televizni-debate-lehci-ton-stridaly-tvrde-utoky|title=Zeman a Schwarzenberg se střetli v druhé televizní debatě. Lehčí tón střídaly tvrdé útoky|date=18 January 2013|work=[[Hospodářské noviny]]|publisher=iHned.cz|language=cs|access-date=22 January 2013}}</ref> Schwarzenberg has been criticized for the fact that his wife cannot speak Czech and that he spent a part of his life abroad, despite the fact that his family fled from communists when he was a child.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.lidovky.cz/klausova-podporila-zemana-nechce-nastupkyni-ktera-mluvi-jen-nemecky-1iw-/zpravy-domov.aspx?c=A130118_211303_ln_domov_mpr|title=Klausová podpořila Zemana. Nechce první dámu, která neumí česky|date=18 January 2013|work=Lidové noviny|publisher=lidovky.cz|language=cs|access-date=22 January 2013}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/schwarzenberga-neprekvapila-klausova-podpora-zemanovi-pjs-/domaci.aspx?c=A130117_141906_domaci_kop|title=Schwarzenberg: Kamarády Klause a Zemana spojují jejich kostlivci|date=17 January 2013|work=Mladá fronta DNES|publisher=iDNES|language=cs|access-date=22 January 2013}}</ref> It was suggested that members of his family collaborated with [[Nazis]], most notably by the son of [[Václav Klaus|the Czech President]], Václav Klaus Jr. These charges have been dismissed by historians.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.lidovky.cz/klaus-junior-nerika-pravdu-otec-schwarzenberga-byl-vlastenec-puu-/zpravy-domov.aspx?c=A130117_140304_ln_domov_vsv|title=Historik: Klaus junior neříká pravdu, otec Schwarzenberga byl vlastenec|date=17 January 2013|work=Lidové noviny|publisher=lidovky.cz|language=cs|access-date=22 January 2013}}</ref> President Václav Klaus, his [[Slovak people|Slovak]] spouse [[Livia Klausová|Livia]] and son Václav expressed their concerns towards Schwarzenberg, pointing to the complete lack of knowledge of the [[Czech language]] of his spouse or to his emigration during the communist era. Schwarzenberg responded that ''"...the last hundred years have demonstrated that an appeal to the lowest instincts has tragic consequences."''<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.rozhlas.cz/zpravy/politika/_zprava/schwarzenberg-zeman-s-klausem-tvori-jednu-mocenskou-skupinu--1164279|title=Schwarzenberg: Zeman s Klausem tvoří jednu mocenskou skupinu|last=Sehnoutka|first=Petr|date=20 January 2012|publisher=[[Czech Radio]]|language=cs|access-date=22 January 2013}}</ref> Additionally, he countered by claiming that the President Klaus and Zeman created a power group and manipulated his claims. He also called their alleged pact a "fraud on the voters".<ref>{{cite web|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/klaus-a-zeman-mocenska-skupina-des-/domaci.aspx?c=A130120_121002_domaci_skr|title= Klaus se Zemanem podvádějí české voliče, zlobí se Schwarzenberg|date=20 January 2013|work=[[Mladá fronta DNES]]|publisher=iDNES|language=cs|access-date=22 January 2013}}</ref> In a leaked text message to a friend, President Klaus wrote that if Karel Schwarzenberg won the election, he would consider emigration.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.novinky.cz/domaci/291359-klaus-potvrdil-pravost-sms-o-emigraci.html|title=Klaus potvrdil pravost SMS o emigraci|date=26 January 2013|publisher=novinky.cz|language=cs|access-date=25 January 2013}}</ref>
[[File:Flag of the President of the Czech Republic.svg|thumb|left|200px|Flag of the president of the Czech Republic with the inscription "[[Truth prevails]]".]]
The critics of Karel Schwarzenberg mentioned his post in the unpopular [[Petr Nečas's Cabinet|cabinet of Petr Nečas]]. Schwarzenberg, leader of a government coalition party [[TOP 09]], a vice-premier and a foreign minister, was frequently associated with the finance minister and his TOP 09 colleague [[Miroslav Kalousek]], one of the key proponents of the austerity measures and spending cuts in the Czech Republic.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.lidovky.cz/zeman-vratil-uder-take-schwarzenberg-hlasoval-pro-nepopularni-reformy-13x-/zpravy-domov.aspx?c=A130112_170149_ln_domov_spa|title=Zeman začal novou kampaň ostře: Schwarzenberg hlasoval pro vyšší DPH|date=12 January 2013|work=Lidové noviny|publisher=lidovky.cz|language=cs|access-date=22 January 2013}}</ref> In the first round, he received the majority of support by voters in [[Bohemia]]n regions and in some of the biggest Czech cities, such as [[Prague]], [[Brno]], and [[Plzeň]].

Miloš Zeman, a former successful politician and [[Czech Social Democratic Party|Social Democratic]] prime minister, announced his comeback and the intention to run in the election in February 2012.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://aktualne.centrum.cz/domaci/politika/clanek.phtml?id=733055|title=Miloš Zeman: Sežeňte podpisy a pokusím se znovu o Hrad|date=14 February 2012|publisher=aktuálně.cz|language=cs|access-date=22 January 2013}}</ref> He narrowly won the first round, supported mainly by voters from industrial regions such as [[North Bohemia]] and [[Czech Silesia|Silesia]], and smaller towns and villages. He has been criticized for the opaque funding of his campaign; the media pointed to his special relationships with controversial business subjects and lobbyists, such as [[Miroslav Šlouf]] and the Russian oil company [[LUKoil]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/zeman-a-jeho-vazby-na-sponzory-deq-/domaci.aspx?c=A120920_212842_domaci_brd|title= Kdo platí Zemanovu kampaň? Šloufovi kamarádi z byznysu|date=21 September 2012|work=[[Mladá fronta DNES]]|publisher=iDNES|access-date=22 January 2013}}</ref> Some of the issues associated with his previous political activities also reappeared in public. During the pre-election debates, Zeman had to face questions about connections between his former chief advisor Šlouf and the alleged mafia kingpin [[František Mrázek]] or about a discrediting campaign against his former colleague, Minister [[Petra Buzková]].

On 22 January, the newspaper ''[[Mladá fronta DNES]]'' reported that the "massive negative campaign" of Miloš Zeman and his team won him popularity in the [[online media]], while Schwarzenberg's supporters have a majority on social sites, such as [[Facebook]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://zpravy.idnes.cz/prezidenstke-volby-a-pruzkum-online-medii-a-socialnich-siti-plz-/domaci.aspx?c=A130121_171910_domaci_ert|title=Média ovládl Zeman s negativní kampaní, Facebook zase Schwarzenberg|date=22 January 2013|work=Mladá fronta DNES|publisher=iDNES|language=cs|access-date=22 January 2013}}</ref>

During the election, the tensions and rivalries in the Czech society and media culminated to an unusual degree.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.lidovky.cz/novy-prezident-zeman-budu-prezidentem-dolnich-deseti-milionu-p6q-/zpravy-domov.aspx?c=A130126_162509_ln_domov_khu|title=Nový prezident Zeman: Budu prezidentem dolních deseti milionů|date=26 January 2013|work=Lidové noviny|publisher=lidovky.cz|access-date=27 January 2013}}</ref> Some of the commentators and politologists pointed to growing polarization of the society, which was also noted by some of the foreign media, such as ''[[The New York Times]]''.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/world/europe/former-prime-minister-is-elected-president-of-czech-republic.html|title=Former Prime Minister Is Elected President of Czech Republic|last=Bilefsky|first=Dan|date=26 January 2013|work=The New York Times|access-date=27 January 2013}}</ref>

On 26 January, Miloš Zeman won the second round of the election. In his first post-election speech, he thanked his supporters and promised to be the president of all people. He also criticized the media that openly supported only one of the candidates.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://aktualne.centrum.cz/prezidentske-volby/clanek.phtml?id=769687|title=Zeman barvy nemění: Zapřel Šloufa a vynadal novinářům|last=Kudláčková|first=Lucie |date=26 January 2013|publisher=aktuálně.cz|language=cs|access-date=27 January 2013}}</ref> ''"Truth and love have finally prevailed over lies and hatred"'', stated the outgoing President Klaus, ironically paraphrasing the renowned Czech statesman (and political opponent) [[Václav Havel]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.radio.cz/en/news|title=Outgoing president Klaus: truth and love prevailed in Miloš Zeman's election (News 27-01-2013)|last=Richter|first=Jan |date=27 January 2013|publisher=[[Czech Radio]]|access-date=27 January 2013}}</ref>

The Austrian press ascribed Zeman's victory to a "dirty [[Anti-German sentiment|anti-German]] campaign."<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.ceskenoviny.cz/news/zpravy/czechs-wasting-chance-to-change-policy-german-handelsblatt/894237|title=Czechs wasting chance to change policy – German Handelsblatt|date=27 January 2013|publisher=České noviny (ČTK)|access-date=30 January 2013}}</ref>

[[Median (agency)|Median]] a Czech agency made a survey to find out what was the reason of the result. According to the survey Zeman was able to gain votes of left-wing supporters of other candidates namely [[Jan Fischer (politician)|Jan Fischer]] and [[Jiří Dienstbier Jr.]] Schwarzenberg on the other hand a little exhausted his electoral base in the first round and lost some supporters during a debate about [[Beneš decrees]] and his membership in [[Petr Nečas' Cabinet]]. According to the survey Zeman was an acceptable candidate for 46% of voters and Schwarzenberg for 35%. 71% of asked expected that the next president will influence the government and will support patriotism.<ref name=duvod>{{cite news|last1=Hyblerová|first1=Lucie|title=gentura uvedla důvod, proč Zeman vyhrál volby|url=http://zpravy.tiscali.cz/agentura-uvedla-duvod-proc-zeman-vyhral-volby-208351|access-date=12 August 2014|agency=Zpravy.tiscali.cz}}</ref>

